## Chapel

::bg{location="chapel" time="night"}
::music{action="start" mood="hush" volume="low"}
@narrator: Six pews, all facing the wrong way: towards the door, towards you.
@narrator: The hymn board still holds three numbers. A bell rope hangs through a hole in the ceiling, frayed to a ponytail at the end. A box of altar matches sits on the lectern.
@nell{mono when="@shaken"}: The pews were turned so the patients could watch the door. So they would see him coming.
@nell{mono}: Mum made us go to chapel at Christmas. Toby used to count the organ pipes. Thirty-one.
